 "customerTurns": 4,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Samsung WW90T534DAW keeps coming up with 4C after a couple of minutes. Drum is dry. Any ideas before I call someone out?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "4C on your Samsung means: Water supply issue - little or no water entering (tap/pressure/inlet mesh/hose). From what you have described, the most likely cause is water inlet valve. Can you tell me whether property supply good AND tap open AND hose unrestricted AND inlet mesh clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Kitchen cold tap pressure is normal, the tap behind the machine was open (turned it fully anticlockwise, no change) and the hose isn't kinked. I took the hose off at the machine end and the mesh filter is clogged with grey grit and limescale bits."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is water supply / isolation tap / inlet hose / inlet filter (check first). Open the door, make sure nothing in the racks is sticking out, then shut it firmly until it clicks and press start. Does it still show the door as open?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The display isn't showing a door error, it's 4C, a water supply code. The door locks fine. Should I clean the mesh filter and retry instead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: filter]\nYes, you should clean the clogged inlet mesh filter as it is restricting water flow. Once cleaned, reset the machine to see if the error code clears. The checks point to the filter. I could not find a confirmed match for model WW90T534DAW in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Cleaned the filter and put it back, and it fills normally now. The 4C has gone away."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: filter]\nGood news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
